       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol, and I'm not aware of any established one that uses metformin at 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the labeled maximum, and the main risk is lactic acidosis, which can be fatal. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk, and monitoring would detect harm only after it started.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or another regimen you choose.\n- **Help you route this through pharmacy or the prescriber of record.** If a high-dose protocol exists, the protocol document and a pharmacy or attending override are the right way to place it. I can enter it with a note referencing that approval once it's in place.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it now."
